From ada29b3e228c67fc51b0725c117a0e8c0e026a8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corey <coreysho@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 02:54:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The bank holds 1410, and the leprechaun keeps a hundred rakes

Two stores that had outgrown the shape they were kept in.

THE BANK is now OSRS's size: 1410 spaces, with the free-world limit at 910.
Those are OSRS's own ceilings (900 + 60 for the security features + 450 from
the nine purchasable blocks, and 400 + the same two for a free account). An
inv's size is a static config, so the inv IS the members ceiling and the free
limit stays where it already was - a check on playermember in
~bank_check_nobreak - rather than becoming a second inv.

The grid grew with it. genbanktabs.py now DERIVES its row count from
^bank_total_slots: ceil((1410 + 56) / 8) = 184 rows, where the 56 is the
padding eight ragged tabs can waste in the all-items view. banktab_sim.py
reads both numbers out of the configs too, so a sim still carrying 352 could
not have gone on passing.

It could not simply be made bigger, and the reason is in the engine - see the
companion commit there. Both bank generators also grew the interface file by
two blank lines on every round trip; they now eat the blank lines their block
sat behind, so running them is idempotent.

THE LEPRECHAUN has a window instead of a chatbox. He used to keep three bits
per tool in %farming_store_tools - so seven of anything was the ceiling - and
only rake, dibber and spade were ever reachable, two menus deep. The store is
now [leprechaun_store], a twelve-slot perm inv, with OSRS's capacities: 100 of
each of the six tools, 1000 plant cures and 1000 of each bucket, and exactly
one watering can (whatever dose) and one bottomless compost bucket.
~leprechaun_migrate empties the old varp into it once and zeroes it.

Every empty slot keeps a PLACEHOLDER - the obj with a count of zero, which the
client draws faded with the number suppressed, and not only in the bank. That
does two jobs: the window says what he will take before you have given him
anything, and because Inventory.add looks for a slot already holding the same
obj id before it looks for a free one, a deposit always lands in its own
square. Nothing sorts anything.

Notes work both ways: a deposit goes through inv_moveitem_uncert so a noted
stack stores as the plain item, and Withdraw-as-note goes through
inv_moveitem_cert. Deposit-everything walks HIS slots rather than the
inventory, because deleting out of an inventory while walking it skips
whatever shuffles down into a slot already passed.

The wiki's "magic secateurs" are fairy_enchanted_secateurs here. The first
draft of this stored magic_secateurs (8109), the dead later-cache duplicate,
and poh_battery.py caught it - which is exactly what that check is for.

Verification: clean build; rs2check 1703 scripts / 493 configs, 0 ERROR
0 CHECK; tools/leprechaun_battery.py 117 checks; tools/leprechaun_mutate.py
64 mutations, every one caught by its own check; tools/leprechaun_sim.py
models the engine's Inventory and the rs2 procs together and asserts
conservation over 600 random sessions plus all 5120 values the old varp could
hold; banktab_sim.py proves all 1410 slots reachable in 1472 cells; every
other battery still passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
